list.item:
Tada outlined the policy of the Japanese Army in China as having eight
                        points: 
                            (a)

Japan’s attitude toward Chinese must always be fair and
                                impartial;
                            (b)

Japan’s policy must be implemented by continual exercising of
                                pressure on China;
                            (c)

commodities must be exchanged freely on a mutually profitable
                                basis;
                            (d)

Japan must respect China’s independence;
                            (e)

Japan must not trust personalities too implicitly;
                            (f)

all new and old military groups in North China and officials who
                                extort money from the people must be eliminated;
                            (g)

Japan must work for the elimination of professional pro-Japanese
                                politicians in China;
                            (h)

both sides must correct mistaken idea of superiority.
